-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Highway Encounter
  Publisher   Vortex, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Highway Encounter (1985)(Vortex).z80
  MD5         ecfe7da10ba9aa395ae54c44301be1af

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The default keeps the original look, and the small colour clash the original
  has stays (see the note). The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. The menu's Presentation line adds more; see the note. Game logic
  is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu, are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Approved figures and scenery colours. Optional, off by default.
              Native editable figure sheet; no new outline. Source: Enhanced
              colours: MatGubbins (Spec256).

  Pace        original

  Note        Original monochrome presentation by default, with original-pace
              drawing windows. Optional approved Enhanced colours preserve the
              original mask/OR depth and clipping. Original loading screen.
              Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: individual updates vary slightly
              with raster phase; measured quiet/busy pace stays within 0.7%.
              Beeper pulse spacing differs by up to 1.715us in tested scenes.
              CPU-only fallback on older cores or hardware-IM2 configurations
              adds up to 46ms at room changes; original-pace acceptance
              applies to the normal DMA path. Missing: natural completion and
              comprehensive collision playthrough, hardware and other-emulator
              testing.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite time
   2  Immunity
   3  Objects: shots only

  Archive POK checked against this exact 48K release. Infinite time; immunity
  in both collision directions; objects only destroyed by shots. Conflicting
  plot-code variants excluded. All off by default.

